    answer:
      "I start with a content inventory — everything the app contains — and the top tasks users come to do, so navigation is built around their goals rather than our org chart. To learn how users think about the content I run card sorting: participants group topics and name the groups, which reveals their mental models and vocabulary. I turn the patterns into a draft hierarchy, then validate it with tree testing, where people find items in a text-only version of the structure, which isolates the IA from visual design. Labels use users' words, frequently used items stay one tap away, and rarely used ones sit deeper with progressive disclosure, with good search as a safety net.",
